See AGENTS.md at the repo root for the authoritative agent guide and target architecture.
Read it before adding or refactoring code.

Key rules: one shared httpx transport injected into every resource and the auth manager;
composition over inheritance (no resource subclasses the HTTP client); a single AuthManager
with no hardcoded URLs; typed return contracts (never leak raw httpx.Response); a KekaError
exception hierarchy. Do NOT extend legacy paths (keka_sdk/hr.py, inheritance resources, dual
auth systems, duplicated types/transport).
